WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.102
-My first guest
is an entrepreneur,

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:05.939
a best-selling cook-book author,
and a social-media icon.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.808
We're gonna get to that.
She's also one of our favorites.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.843
You can check out
her new online store

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:15.114
Cravings Shop
at cravingsbychrissyteigen.com

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.683
Here is Chrissy Teigen!

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.986
Ahh! Come on!
-Thank you! Whoo!

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.256
-Look at you.
-Can I -- I need to walk out.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.992
-I know. Maybe we can, like --

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.427
-It makes me sad. It's okay.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.329
-We can get you some
walk-out music for that.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:31.864
Come on.
-I'll trip over something.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.399
-Thank you for doing this.
-Hi.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.600
-You look fantastic.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.202
I actually miss
seeing your face.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.238
-Thank you.
-I wanted to ask you about this.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.608
You were one of the 13 people
that the President --

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.842
President Biden
followed on Twitter

00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:45.645
with the official
@POTUS account.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.882
I was so excited that you --
I was like, "This is so cool."

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.719
'Cause, honestly, you're so
refreshing and fun on socials.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.121
And you were very excited
about it, too.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.656
But then a few weeks later --
-So excited.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.224
-And this is why I love you --

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.093
You asked the President
to unfollow you.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.728
Do you remember --
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.430
-Do you remember
the exact moment you thought

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.968
that that was a bad idea to have
President Biden follow you?

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.637
-The second it happened,
I was like, "Oh [bleep]."

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:14.473
And I truly -- I think
I sent like two tweets --

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.209
Sorry. Sorry.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.211
I sent like two tweets
in, like, two weeks,

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:20.947
and people were worried.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.782
They were like,
"What is going on?"

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.584
And, like, listen, I know --
I don't believe

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.552
that he thought -- maybe --
I don't believe he's like Trump

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.354
and actively
really scrolling through,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.256
but it was so amazing
that he followed me

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.992
'cause I had been shunned
for -- for four years.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.729
I couldn't see anything
that was being said, and I --

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.466
So it was -- it was --
I loved the statement of that.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.568
But then it just became
too much.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:46.939
And, also, when you're on that
list, a bunch of weird people

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:48.975
go to his account,
and they don't know you at all,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.509
so they're like,
"Who's this chick?"

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:53.746
And then they come to my page,
and it's just a hellhole.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.147
-[ Laughs ] Oh, please.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.982
-So it was like --
It was really --

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:58.952
It was so much better.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.053
Yeah, so life is better now.

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.188
-Were you so excited
at the inauguration?

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:07.593
Was that -- Or was it just
freezing or was it both?

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:11.631
-Oh, inauguration was freezing
and amazing and beautiful.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.999
And I didn't know
that John's performance

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:16.769
at the Washington Monument
was a secret,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.105
so I Instagrammed
the whole thing,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.541
like, the day before
for rehearsal.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.976
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.
-And then I got in trouble.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.745
-"Oops." [ Laughs ]
-Oh, my God.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.848
I remember I was so scared
'cause I --

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.717
We ran into Katy Perry after.
And I always say dumb things.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.687
Like, I always get so nervous
and I say faux pas.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.856
I hadn't seen Katy for so long.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:42.328
And I was like, "Oh,
I typically hate fireworks...

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.830
but that was, like, amazing.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.332
That was beautiful."

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.268
And then I think
she heard that I said

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.003
I hate "Firework,"
like, the song.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.772
-Yeah. Like, "That's my song."

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.408
-And so -- I know!
And I wanted to die!

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.076
I felt so bad.
-"That's not what I meant."

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.777
-I was like,
"No, no, no, not 'Fireworks.'"

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:00.746
Ugh! I always do that.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:02.982
-But I kind of agree with you
on fireworks.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.251
I think they go on
a little too long for me.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:09.422
-Yes. They don't -- Yeah, it's
like bad improv or something,

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.123
and it's like two minutes
too long.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.758
And I don't get fountains,
either.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.194
Fountains and fireworks
are just two nos for me.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.264
-[ Laughs ] Yeah. Fountains.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.866
I wouldn't invest in a fountain.
I don't mind looking at one.

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:23.202
I just don't -- I don't if I --
-I don't get it.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.437
I just don't get -- The Grove.
The people at the Grove

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.440
that sit around and take
pictures around the fountain --

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.709
It's like -- It's a hose.
I don't get it.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:34.346
-I want to talk about
"Cravings."

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:36.215
I want to talk
about your cookbook.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.150
You're finishing up
your third cookbook.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.752
Congrats on this.
-Yeah, thanks.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.555
-There's going to be 100 recipes
in this thing.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:47.259
-I had 99 recipes,
and so, for 100, I just, like,

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:50.128
buttered a bunch of Gardetto's
and stuffed it in a pita.

00:03:50.128 --> 00:03:52.631
And then it was supposed to be,
like, a joke recipe,

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:55.735
but then we --
it's actually really good.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.370
-Oh, really?
-But I promise the rest

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.471
of the recipes are really
serious and they're good.

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.240
-No, I follow you,
and I see what you do.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.975
You actually --
You go for it, by the way.

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.912
And I love
that you test everything.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:09.081
Can you talk about the mandolin
and trying that for the --

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.983
-Oh!
-Was it Super Bowl Sunday?

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.484
-That was the Super Bowl.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:16.555
-Super Bowl Sunday, John --
I brought a mandolin at Ralph's,

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.225
and we were making
scalloped potatoes.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.461
And John was watching the game
and doing the mandolin,

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.962
and you just --
That's a big no-no.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.664
You can't watch anything
while doing it.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.866
And he sliced off
the tip of his finger.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:30.036
And fingers are all John needs
in life, basically,

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:33.405
so I was like, "You idiot!"

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.341
He started running it
under water,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.710
and he was like, "I'm not gonna
go to the emergency room.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.112
I want to watch the game."

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.547
So it's just flapping around,
his finger.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.483
And I was like,
"You idiot, give it to me."

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.185
And then I did one pass,

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.155
and I chopped off
the tip of my finger, too,

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.623
and then I dragged him
to the emergency room.

00:04:51.623 --> 00:04:54.026
-We have a photo.
-I brought him to the E.R.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.794
-We have a photo of you guys.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:59.131
That's you at the hospital.
That's you at the hospital.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.133
-I brought him so we could
get special treatment.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.302
I drag John everywhere
so I can get better treatment.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.237
-Winners, man. Thumbs up,
and a finger up like,

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.172
"Hey, number one, man."
-Yep.

00:05:07.172 --> 00:05:08.641
-Hey, pal.
I want to show you something.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.376
Look at this.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.944
I want to talk about
the Cravings Shop.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.613
-Aah! Yes!

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:17.216
-Dude, talk to me about this.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.351
-The chocolates are, honestly,
so incredible.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:22.855
They're all my recipes inside
a Compartes chocolate bar,

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.790
which is already, like, so --

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.159
I learned that I fell in love
with white chocolate.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:28.594
Theirs is so creamy
and delicious.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.630
And my famous banana bread
is crumbled up into it.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.533
And carrot cake.
And it's just so delicious.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.737
We have, you know, the crystals
that are so much fun to wear.

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:40.206
I decided in this pandemic
that you're wearing a mask,

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:43.042
and I'm just very into
wearing something

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.610
with some kind of flair,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.445
and so we did
these beautiful crystals.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.948
My friend, Nova, did them,
and they're so awesome.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:51.617
And, honestly, they're not

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.452
just for Coachella anymore,
I decided.

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:56.322
I want to actively wear
crystals.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:59.291
-Let me see.
Are they hard to wear?

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.194
-[ Laughs ] I love you.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.429
-Let's see.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.064
-It's beautiful!
-Oh, thank you.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:09.167
-Oh, my God! See?
-It's good. I like it.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:12.205
And it's, like, kind of subtle,
but it's beautiful,

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:14.840
and, honestly,
it makes me feel good.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.043
I love it.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.911
-Don't you just feel better?

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:22.648
-Dude, I do feel better.
-Chrissy, sales are down.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:26.618
-Wait. Sales are down.
Take the crystals off, Jimmy.

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:28.854
Exactly.
You don't want me as a model.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.323
I'll tell you what, though.
I don't know if a lot

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:34.427
of people realize how much work
goes into these things,

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.862
to even have your name
on one thing.

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:40.166
I know you. We've known
each other for a long time now.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:41.367
This is years in the making.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.002
It's not like,
"Oh, hey, Chrissy,

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.003
in two months,
just put your name on this."

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:46.672
You go, "No, no, no.
I got to do this..."

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:49.409
-Yeah, I'm telling you.
It's years, years, years.

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.511
So when it does come out,
it seems like,

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:52.945
"Oh, surprise, it's a shop."

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:56.149
But, yeah, it's a lot
of hard work, so thank you.

00:06:56.149 --> 00:07:00.619
It's my baby, and I -- Yeah,
we're a small little company,

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.688
and it's just really fun
to do it all.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.156
-Good for you guys.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:08.060
I got the latest addition
to the Cravings Shop,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.596
and this is very you.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.330
You have your own line of robes.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.233
-[ Laughs ] I have robes.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.668
That's the Basic Bitch Terry.

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:19.071
-[ Laughs ]
Is that what it's called?

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.907
-Yeah, it's just basic.
I didn't want bulky pockets.

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:24.143
I didn't want a tie
that would fall off.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:26.478
I didn't want anything --
It's just a basic-ass --

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:28.414
[ Laughs ]

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:32.351
-Do you just wear this
around the house and stuff?

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:35.855
-Yes, it's so --
It's really short, too.

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.123
-It is tiny.

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:40.693
-No. Well, you're tall, so
it's going to be short on you.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.362
But, yeah, you can roll up
the sleeves, wear your crystals.

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.531
I love you.
-No, this is fantastic.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.566
It is a little short,
but I think --

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:49.535
You know what?
It's a little sexy.

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:50.803
-You're tall.
-This is --

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.838
No, no. This is the new --
-That's the thing.

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.874
Those robes are usually
bulky and lame,

00:07:55.874 --> 00:07:58.043
so I wanted it
to have some sex appeal.

00:07:58.043 --> 00:08:00.579
"I've given up,
but not entirely."

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:02.548
That's what it says.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:03.615
That's a robe that screams

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:05.417
"I've given up,
but not entirely."

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:07.953
-I love the Basic Bitch Terry.

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:10.989
You have the cookbook.
You have all this cooking stuff.

00:08:10.989 --> 00:08:14.993
Will there ever be
a Chrissy Teigen restaurant?

00:08:14.993 --> 00:08:17.095
-Oh, my God! There is --

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:19.164
We are chatting about it
right now,

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:22.701
and I have looked
at some incredible spaces.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:25.071
I don't know if it's so much
a restaurant as it is,

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:29.408
you know, a sitdown,
fast, casual establishment.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.678
But I have dreams of, like,
a beautiful mezzanine

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.146
and John playing the piano

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:35.714
and it raining down
on the block.

00:08:35.714 --> 00:08:38.317
I mean, I really -- I just want
to pretty much live there

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.919
and take pictures
with people and -- Yeah.

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:44.723
-I think this is a good start
right here. Congrats.

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:47.192
Chrissy Teigen, everybody.

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:51.564
Check out her Cravings Shop
at cravingsbychrissyteigen.com.

